content.text:
The build fails because `Celebracion` uses `Math.random()` during prerender. The `useMemo` with `[activo]` still executes during SSR render. Fix: generate confetti positions in a `useEffect` (client only) or lazily on mount with useState. Use:

```tsx
const [piezas, setPiezas] = useState<Array<...>>([]);
useEffect(() => {
  if (activo) {
    setPiezas(Array.from({length: PIEZAS}, (_, i) => ({...})));
  } else {
    setPiezas([]);
  }
}, [activo]);
```

That defers randomness to client. Update component and remove the eslint-disable comment (no longer needed). Also remove useMemo import.

